# Builds

- The repository is untrusted; repository code runs only inside `docker build`. `internal/build` reads the checkout only through `repoFS` (`os.Root`, every path component `Lstat`ed: symbolic links and non-regular files refused, size caps per file) and only `golem-deploy.yaml`, `.dockerignore`, `golem.yaml`, `go.mod`, `package.json`, lockfile/command directory existence and a custom Dockerfile. Never write to the checkout; never read other repository files on the host (no Go source parsing, no executing anything).
- `ParseConfig` is strict (`KnownFields`, one document, 64 KiB); paths pass `cleanPath` (segment allowlist `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`, no `.`/`..`/`.git`, no leading `-`), commands and args pass `checkWords` (no control/bidi characters). `Dockerfile` re-validates every plan value and renders commands only through `execForm` (JSON, one line); `checkLines` and the golden files in `testdata/golden` pin the output (`go test ./internal/build -run Dockerfile -update` after an intended change). Messages to users are `*UserError` (no host paths, no command output; repository-derived names go through `safePath`/`logsafe.String`).
- `Inspect` is the preflight (engine `>= MinEngineVersion` via `golang.org/x/mod/semver`, `ValidEngineVersion`, no local/root replace of engine modules, Go image version from `go`/`toolchain`, server package detection, npm dirs, web build, `BakeCheck` when any golem.yaml output exists).
- `Service.Run` is the `project.build` job body: optional `prepare` (the pull), daemon-wide `slot` (one build at a time), `MarkBuildRunning`, `--build-timeout`, private dir `tmp/build-<id>-*` (Dockerfile, `Dockerfile.dockerignore` = repo `.dockerignore` + `MandatoryIgnores`, `static/` from `stageAddons` with `internal/extract`), `docker.Client.Build`, `BuiltImage` verification, `FinishBuild`, `retain`. Every exit records the build (`run.finish`); `Watch` (started by the handler with the job's `Done`) releases the `Reserve` place (`MaxActiveBuilds`) and records builds whose job never ran. Cache mount ids are `golem-deploy-<hash of instance id>-p<project>-<what>` (the Dockerfile is shown in build logs; never put the instance id itself there).
- `internal/docker/build.go`: `BuildSpec.Args` is the only argv (pinned in `build_test.go`); labels come from the CLI (`BuildSpec.Labels`), `BuildEnv` is fixed (`DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1`, `BUILDX_GIT_INFO=false`, no attestations). Never add `--build-arg`, `--secret`, `--ssh`, `--allow`, `--network`. `BuiltImage` resolves the iidfile (classic store) or `containerimage.digest` (containerd store) as exact ids and requires exactly the build's `dev.golemengine.deploy.*` labels (`ErrLabelMismatch`: the caller removes the image); servers re-check the same set before every run (`BuildImage`). `TestBuildToServer` (fake Docker) and `TestBuiltImageAndBuildImageAgree` keep both sides in agreement.
- Build output goes through `logsafe.Writer` with host-path redactions; never put it in `CmdError.Detail`, job details or responses.
- One image rule everywhere (build deletion, retention, project deletion, `DELETE /images`, `Image.in_use`): an image is in use while a successful build records it or any container was created from it (`docker.ContainersUsingImage`/`ImagesInUse`; stopped server containers count, a server switched to another build keeps its old container until its next start). Deletion (`Service.Delete`, retention) goes through `store.DeleteBuildUnused` (refuses active builds and builds `servers.build_id` references), keeps images another successful build records (`CountBuildsWithImage`), refuses with `*ImageInUseError` (server ids of the containers) while a container uses the image, deletes the row before the image (best effort, logged). Deleting a project is refused while servers use its builds (`DeleteProjectUnused`) or containers use their images (`CheckProjectImages`) and removes its images afterwards (`RemoveImages`).
- Static add-ons: `projects.static_addons` JSON (`store.StaticAddon`), validated by `build.ValidateAddons` (names via `staticfiles.ValidateName`, `.zip`, targets via `cleanPath`, max 16); PATCH checks the files exist and are ZIPs; `DELETE /static/{name}` is refused while `store.ProjectsUsingStatic` finds a user.
- HTTP (`handlers_builds.go`): POST holds `projectState.mu`, refuses without checkout unless `pull`, reserves, creates the row, starts the job (subject project, `jobs.InPool(build.JobPool)`), `SetBuildJob`, `Watch`. Routes: `POST|GET /projects/{id}/builds` (developer), `GET /builds`, `GET /builds/{id}` (developer), `DELETE /builds/{id}` (admin).
- Verify with `go test ./internal/build/... ./internal/docker/... ./internal/httpapi/... ./internal/store/...`; with Docker `GOLEM_DEPLOY_DOCKER_TESTS=1 go test -p 1 ./internal/build/...` (builds and runs `testdata/game`, needs network; exec-form round trip; custom Dockerfile context/entitlement/label checks). Symlink tests skip on Windows without symlink privileges; run them on Linux.
